## One understandable water lift

Waterwheel + Glazed clay jar → Waterwheel with jars replaces Wheel + Hollow pipe → Pump and Pump + Waterwheel → Water pump. The existing Reservoir then takes the jar-wheel, and the channel/irrigated-garden goals remain exact. Canonical route 224 → 223 actions; all thirty chapters, locations, stock, goals, hotspots and milestones are unchanged. Hollow pipe still serves channel and filtration; wheel still serves mill gearing; ceramic service alternatives remain.

A noria uses containers around a water-driven wheel rim to lift water into receiving storage. The selected principle has primary support, but lift range depends on wheel geometry and operation. Ordinary fixing/alignment and the existing plural pottery-supply abstraction are compressed; this game does not specify dimensions, flow, safety or real construction performance. [FAO, Water lifting devices §3.4.1](https://www.fao.org/4/ah810e/AH810E05.htm).

The old generic pump is not declared physically impossible. The bounded design finding was that its smooth wheel and open conduit did not visibly choose a lifting mechanism. The new familiar inputs provide that principle without a machinery checklist. This is a supported AI design inference, not demonstrated human understanding or enjoyment.

